    "title": "Kernel module loaded or unloaded",
    "desc": "A program loaded or unloaded a kernel module - insmod, rmmod, modprobe, kmod. Code running in the kernel can hide processes, files and network connections and survive a reboot, so a loadable kernel module is a top-tier rootkit mechanism (Diamorphine, libprocesshider's kin) and a persistence foothold (MITRE T1547.006 / T1014). On a host whose module set is fixed at boot by its NixOS configuration, a hand-run insmod/modprobe outside that is off-pattern.",
